263	HTI	GGXWDG	Haiti	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2014/15 Notes: General Government only includes Central Government Start/end months of reporting year: October/September GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government; Valuation of public debt: Nominal value Primary domestic currency: Haitian gourde Data last updated: 03/2016	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	23.172	25.012	27.592	42.860	42.431	51.038	74.214	70.049	79.244	77.108	75.968	95.238	74.413	46.292	35.758	53.623	78.224	103.027	128.123	168.284	190.028	208.331	222.408	231.001	238.910	2015
