917	KGZ	GGXWDG	Kyrgyz Republic	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2014 Start/end months of reporting year: January/December GFS Manual used: Not reported according to GFS Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government;Local Government;Social Security Funds; Valuation of public debt: Face value Primary domestic currency: Kyrgyz som Data last updated: 03/2016	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	79.915	79.288	80.542	89.655	87.660	86.713	82.504	80.605	91.098	116.843	131.619	141.223	152.053	163.800	210.694	291.258	339.362	378.873	415.334	451.089	490.160	513.607	2014
