862	WSM	NGDP_FY	Samoa	Gross domestic product corresponding to fiscal year, current prices	Gross domestic product corresponding to fiscal year is the country?s GDP based on the same period during the year as their fiscal data. In the case of countries whose fiscal data are based on a fiscal calendar (e.g., July to June), this series would be the country?s GDP over that same period. For countries whose fiscal data are based on a calendar year (i.e., January to December), this series will be the same as their GDP in current prices.	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2014/15. Fiscal year used Start/end months of reporting year: July/June GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Accrual General government includes: Central Government Primary domestic currency: Samoa tala Data last updated: 02/2016	0.117	0.123	0.148	0.175	0.206	0.237	0.251	0.263	0.288	0.321	0.421	0.423	0.476	0.509	0.400	0.598	0.635	0.717	0.789	0.787	0.845	0.936	1.004	1.082	1.193	1.328	1.425	1.530	1.696	1.661	1.623	1.765	1.843	1.839	1.866	1.946	1.990	2.026	2.115	2.220	2.329	2.444	2015
